            <ArticleTitle>[The role of the nurse in the therapeutic education of patients at high risk of anaphylaxis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>48-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Allergies are common discases which affect 20 to 25% of the French population. The major risks are anaphylactic shock, laryngeal oedema and acute severe asthma. A process of therapeutic education helps to limit these risks for the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
